# BMW 5 Series G30 four-door saloon, 2017-2023.
#
# The seventh 5-series: the CLAR-platform car that replaced the F10, sold as
# saloon and Touring, facelifted in 2020.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_5_Series_(G30)
#
# Dimensions 4.936 x 1.868 x 1.466 m, wheelbase 2.975 m, G30 saloon, from the
# English Wikipedia dimension box. Mirrors take the modelled width to 2.130 m.
#
# Colours: from the BMW UK 5 Series Saloon and Touring brochure, November 2020,
# page 16 and the paintwork ordering table, a primary UK source:
#   Alpine White            300
#   Black Sapphire meta.    475
#   Glacier Silver meta.    A83  (SE trim only in that brochure)
#   Bluestone metallic      C2Y
# The brochure establishes UK offering in November 2020, not the full 2017-2023
# range; per-colour years are not established. Mediterranean Blue and Imperial
# Blue are left out because their later UK availability was not established.
# Weights black 3, blue 3, silver 2, white 2, total 10, provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 250 km/h, the electronic limiter that applies across the range. Comfort
# 140/390, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 140, the same as the E32 and a step above the
# F10's 135/385. Classes 2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: March 2017 intro, retires staggered 2032-2035 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-g30.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-g30.dae (64 objects). References:
# citycars/references/bmw-g30/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the roof and
# body contours are more angular than the photographs, the kidney outlines are
# rectangular rather than rounded, and the nose curvature is simplified. The
# builder flagged these and did not certify Gate B. At 128 px the stance, the
# separate boot and the wraparound lamps read correctly.

obj=citycar
name=BMW5G30(BlackSapphire)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2017
intro_month=3
retire_year=2035
retire_month=6
speed=250
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=140
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=390

